For regular in-person classes I used to check that every student had all th=
e supplies and one lost 10 points if one did not meet the criteria. I have =
found that there is a very high correlation between those who do not pass T=
est 0 and lose 10 points and those who perform very poorly in the course.



This was Test 0 because the students had to pay very careful attention to t=
he definitions so that the item they procured actually satisfied the defini=
ng conditions. This is very good practice for mathematics because language =
is used in a very strict and precise manner in mathematics. If we want a co=
mputer to do something, we must learn to instruct it in a completely unambi=
guous manner.



For online classes, I can neither check anything nor indeed enforce anythin=
g.  The most important thing is for you to obtain a good ruler for drawing =
straight lines and also a mechanical pencil with lead of appropriate diamet=
er (.5mm, .7mm etc.) and softness (2B, 3B, etc.)  so that your work is easi=
ly visible and legible. This is the case if you print out the exam and writ=
e on it. You need to try different things to see if the writing is dark eno=
ugh and also if you break the lead too frequently. Please switch to a thick=
er lead, if the thinner one breaks too often. Usually pencils come with HB =
lead and, therefore, you will need to replace the lead with 2B, 3b, 4B etc.=
 ALL STRAIGHT LINE SEGMENTS OTHER THAN ONES EXPLICITLY EXCLUDED MUST BE DRA=
WN WITH A RULER. ONE WILL LOSE 1 POINT FOR EACH VIOLATION. Please read the =
next paragraph if you are using some device to write on a tablet.



I do not have direct knowledge of most of the writing devices that are curr=
ently in use. If one uses a stylus on a tablet of some sort and if one can =
do everything that one can do with a pencil, a ruler, and a piece of paper,=
 then that should be fine. IT IS VERY IMPORTANT THAT ALL STRAIGHT LJNES (CO=
NCLUSION BARS, BRACKETS FOR MATRICES AND SO ON) ARE VISIBLY STRAIGHT BECAUS=
E THEY ARE DRAWN WITH A RULER OR SOME SUITABLE SOFTWARE.



Some pages from student exams with writing done in HB lead are scarcely leg=
ible. I instituted the rules precisely because it is very difficult to read=
 what students have written if they use HB lead. If you follow the requirem=
ents (which, I hope you do) then you will become organised before you know.=
 This will save you a lot of time and many carry these habits into future c=
lasses. Once you upload your exam please make sure that they are legible an=
d that they are not too large. You may have to reduce scanning resolution t=
o reduce the size. Let me tentatively set the upper limit for the size of a=
n uploaded exam (which must be a single document) to 10 MB. If I find a mor=
e precise estimate I will announce it later.



I do not like many of the features on CANVAS; I neither chose the setup nor=
 wrote the code. But I can learn the syntax (and the hieroglyphics on MS Ou=
tlook) if adequate documentation is provided. Test 0 introduces one to the =
elementary mental discipline necessary to make one pay attention to minute =
details of syntax.



In actual fact, I do not have such documentation for CANVAS, but rely on se=
arching on Google to see find an algorithm for doing what I want to do. The=
se symbols are conventional and must be defined in order that one know the =
meaning. I find the claim that these are intuitively clear not just prepost=
erous but harmful because it is false and imposes an arbitrary setup (that =
may be improved upon) under false pretenses. This is precisely why I have, =
unlike CANVAS, given you a list of symbols and their definitions.



One can be expected to deduce logical consequences. One cannot be expected =
to deduce arbitrary conventions. We shall have occasion to discuss logical =
implication in Discrete Mathematics. You should consider the following ques=
tion: If you see a picture of a human being on a door, does it follow logic=
ally that there is a toilet on the other side?

